Weighted metric facility-location single replacement

There are 26 facilities, with integer IDs 0 through 25.
They form 13 complementary pairs.  Coordinates i=0,...,10
are ordinary pairs; the last two pairs are named z and y.  In every pair the
first displayed ID is the positive literal and the second is its complement.

For ordinary coordinates, indexed from 0 at the LEFT of every orientation row:
POSITIVE_IDS=16,19,25,1,2,10,20,4,12,0,8
NEGATIVE_IDS=21,14,24,18,6,23,15,13,7,3,17
z_pair=22,5
y_pair=9,11

The currently open set contains the negative ID of every pair (including z and y):
CURRENT_OPEN=3,5,6,7,11,13,14,15,17,18,21,23,24

This compact specification defines the complete MUFL instance.  It is not an
approximation.  There is one client co-located with every literal facility; every
such client has integer weight W=1433562023400.  Every facility
has opening cost 2W=2867124046800.

There are also weighted clause clients.  A clause client is specified by two
literal-facility IDs a,b.  Its distance is 4/3 from a and b, 5/3 from the
complementary facilities mate(a),mate(b), and 2 from every other facility.
A literal client has distance 0 from its own facility, 1 from its complement,
and 2 from every other facility.  Distinct clause clients are distance 2 from
one another.  Together with symmetry and distance 0 on identical points, these
rules define the metric.  The cost of an open set is opening cost plus, for every
client, its weight times its distance to the nearest open facility.

Here is the exact clause-client rule.  Put p=11, d=4,
B=325808497, and s=843.  For each ordinary coordinate i
and each orientation line below, create two distinct clients.  If row[i]=1,
create (positive_i,z_positive) with weight high and
(negative_i,z_positive) with weight B.  If row[i]=0, exchange those two
weights.  The row index convention is inclusive and 0-based.

ORIENTATION_ROWS
bit=3 delta=6744 high=325815241 row=01100000010
bit=2 delta=3372 high=325811869 row=10000011001
bit=1 delta=1686 high=325810183 row=10001100011
bit=0 delta=843 high=325809340 row=11001001100

For every ordinary i also create (negative_i,z_positive) with threshold weight
C=2530.  Camouflage rule: none.
Each camouflage r creates both (positive_i,z_positive) and
(negative_i,z_positive) with the same stated weight.  Finally create the guard
client (z_negative,y_positive) with weight L=14335620234.
Thus there are exactly M=100 clause clients.  Repeated literal
pairs denote distinct clients and are allowed.

Task: replace exactly one currently open facility by exactly one currently
closed facility so that the exact MUFL cost strictly decreases.  Order matters:
write the closed ID first and the newly opened ID second.  IDs cannot repeat.

Give your final answer inside <answer></answer> tags, as two decimal integers
close_id, open_id.  Example: <answer>7, 12</answer>
Output nothing else inside the tags.

