The audit found a real G4 flaw in the draft: once the heavy literal-client bound is noticed, only complementary-pair swaps remain, so its honest search space was about 2,000—not four million—and the family was guessable at roughly \(5\times10^{-4}\). I’m replacing the explicit row matrix with a compact, paper-licensed MUFL construction over more than a million complementary pairs; this keeps the two-ID witness fixed while making the structure-aware space genuinely exceed \(10^6\).
