codex
The first oracle call is still computing; there has been no API error or verdict yet. The hardening harness has its own hard wall-clock deadline and will redraw failures rather than counting service errors as mathematical failures.
diff --git a/gen_1612_01752.py b/gen_1612_01752.py
index f5f2a1b1a57bde020c610f975c58ff8311dec870..31f950fba18f1bde6dae1550e41af82a7a79fc98
--- a/gen_1612_01752.py
+++ b/gen_1612_01752.py
@@ -1,9 +1,8 @@
-"""Verified Track-B generator for a single-swap MUFL improvement problem.
+"""Track-B generator for an improving single replacement in weighted MUFL.
 
-The construction is the tight PLS reduction in Section 3 of Brauer,
-arXiv:1612.01752.  A locally improving Boolean flip is carried to a locally
-improving facility swap.  The improving flip is planted by an invertible
-change of variables; no generated instance is solved to obtain its answer.
+The metric is the tight PLS reduction in Section 3 of Brauer (arXiv:1612.01752).
+A unique improving Boolean flip is planted through a hidden affine cube; the
+paper's Proposition 3 and Lemma 5 carry it to an improving facility swap.
