## Caveats

This is Track B, so a CAS or a short program that extracts the affine cube makes
the family easy; that is the intended contrast, not an omitted attack. The exact
G4 density is under a uniform prior on already-deduced complementary flips, not
on all open/closed ID pairs, and therefore does not model a symbolic algebra
solver. The panel did not run a general MILP/SMT package because exact candidate
enumeration is the stronger successful reference algorithm for this compact
subfamily. The paper gives worst-case PLS hardness, not average-case hardness for
these inverse-generated cubics. Finally, G9 is still incomplete for the external
reason above, so this result is not yet submission-ready.
